From c4d49036d9ad9f322be448488482e2f160ff5646 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 01:36:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix sync across different networks: relay-based infohash
 rendezvous

Each device seeds its own torrent with a unique infohash, and infohashes were
only exchanged via the LAN UDP beacon, so trackers/DHT could never connect
devices on different networks. Add a pub/sub rendezvous (ntfy protocol) that
carries 'board X = infohash H' between devices, on desktop and Android, plus
tracker list additions, merge back-off, docs and an end-to-end test.
